  "title": "Random Permutations Fixing k-Sets",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $p(k)$ be the limit as $n \\to \\infty$ of the probability that a random permutation on $[n]$ preserves some set of size $k$. Is $p(k)$ a decreasing function of $k$? Is $p(k) = (C + o(1))k^{-\\alpha}(\\log k)^{-3/2}$ for some absolute constant $C$?",
